    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Stacked on #137 (which is stacked on #136); retarget to `main` as they merge.\n- Brings back the nano-style `M-x` that was removed from `sp-mini-frame` while it was being made to work, now on the posframe:\n  - the prompt in inverse bold with a one-pixel box (`sp-posframe-nano-commands`);\n  - the dotted line under the input (`sp-posframe-divider-char`, `-divider-priority`), in the divider colour of `sp-nano-style`. It has 300 characters and `truncate-lines` is on in that minibuffer, so the window cuts it and it no longer wraps in a narrow frame;\n  - the dimming of the frame behind `sp-select-note`, `sp-insert-note` and `sp-collec-query-select-note` (`sp-posframe-dim-functions`).\n- Not brought back: the colour handling (#121/#123) and the computed fixed height, which only existed to work around `mini-frame`.\n- Styling runs in `condition-case`, so an error cannot stop the prompt.\n- Docs (`sp-posframe.org`, dividers guide) and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Not run in Emacs (none in the container).\n- Whether the box, the line and the colours look right in the posframe on macOS is unconfirmed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
